      "position": 3,
      "content": "CONCENTRATIONS Students in this major are required to choose one of the following concentrations: General Political Science Law and Politics MAJOR INFORMATION The major in political science is designed for students who desire a liberal arts program with an emphasis on politics, government and public policy; plan a career in government service or public administration; seek training for positions in foreign service agencies of the United States government, international organizations or corporations; intend to study law; wish to prepare for teaching in the public schools; or intend to work for advanced degrees in political science in preparation for college or university teaching or for government service. ALL MAJOR REQUIREMENTS The complete list of major requirements is available here: http://bulletin.csusb.edu/colleges-schools-departments/social-behavioral-sciences/political-science/political-science-ba/ CSUSB ADVISING PODCASTS Find out more about this major here: What is the Political Science Major? ASSOCIATE DEGREE FOR TRANSFER (ADTs) This major is similar to the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Political Science. Completion of the ADT guarantees that students will be able to graduate from a similar-designated major at CSUSB in no more than 60 semester units. The ADT does not guarantee that all lower-division requirements are met. Community college transfer students with a compatible ADT MUST meet with an academic advisor early in their first term and each subsequent term to stay on track for graduation.",
      "contentHtml": "<h2>CONCENTRATIONS</h2><p>Students in this major are required to choose one of the following concentrations:</p><ul><li>General Political Science</li><li>Law and Politics</li></ul><p><br></p><h2>MAJOR INFORMATION</h2><p>The major in political science is designed for students who desire a liberal arts program with an emphasis on politics, government and public policy; plan a career in government service or public administration; seek training for positions in foreign service agencies of the United States government, international organizations or corporations; intend to study law; wish to prepare for teaching in the public schools; or intend to work for advanced degrees in political science in preparation for college or university teaching or for government service.</p><p><br></p><h2>ALL MAJOR REQUIREMENTS</h2><p>The complete list of major requirements is available here: <a href=\"http://bulletin.csusb.edu/colleges-schools-departments/social-behavioral-sciences/political-science/political-science-ba/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">http://bulletin.csusb.edu/colleges-schools-departments/social-behavioral-sciences/political-science/political-science-ba/</a></p><p><br></p><h2>CSUSB ADVISING PODCASTS</h2><p>Find out more about this major here:</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://csusbadvising.buzzsprout.com/1215218/12300632-ep-42-what-is-the-political-science-major\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">What is the Political Science Major?</a></li></ul><p><br></p><h2>ASSOCIATE DEGREE FOR TRANSFER (ADTs)</h2><p>This major is similar to the Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Political Science.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion of the ADT guarantees that students will be able to graduate from a similar-designated major at CSUSB in no more than 60 semester units. The ADT does not guarantee that all lower-division requirements are met.</p><p><br></p><p class=\"highlight\"><strong>Community college transfer students with a compatible ADT <u>MUST</u> meet with an academic advisor early in their first term and each subsequent term to stay on track for graduation.</strong></p>"
